---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CTASection from '../../components/CTASection.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Real Estate IT & AI Services" description="AI-powered automation for real estate firms. Automate lead nurturing, tenant communication, document processing, CRM workflows, and property listings. Close deals faster.">

  <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════
       Section 1: Hero
       ════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero__glow hero__glow--1"></div>
    <div class="hero__glow hero__glow--2"></div>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero__content hero-animate">
        <span class="section-label">Real Estate</span>
        <h1 class="hero__title">You're losing deals because leads get lost. Tenants aren't hearing from you. Closings move at a crawl.</h1>
        <p class="hero__subtitle">Real estate is relationship-driven, but right now your relationships live in three different spreadsheets and someone's email inbox. Constance IT automates the workflows that keep deals moving and tenants happy: lead nurturing, tenant communication, document processing, and CRM management.</p>
        <div class="hero__actions">
          <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn--primary">Get a Free Assessment</a>
          <a href="#what-we-automate" class="btn btn--ghost">See Our Real Estate Solutions</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════
       Section 2: The Problem
       ════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="re-problem animate-on-scroll">
        <span class="section-label">The Problem</span>
        <h2>Great leads are disappearing. Documents are bottlenecking closings. Your CRM is out of sync with reality.</h2>
        <p class="text-large">You're getting leads from the web, referrals, and social — but some fall through because follow-up is inconsistent. It takes three emails before a lead actually hears from you. Tenants have questions and can't reach anyone. Documents for closings get emailed back and forth, tracked in multiple places, held up by missing signatures.</p>
        <p class="text-large">Your CRM has all the data, but nobody's entering it in real time. Properties get listed on some sites but not others. Rent collection reminders go out manually, if at all. Property maintenance requests sit in email threads instead of a system.</p>
        <p class="text-large">You're working harder, not smarter. Commissions are available if you could just keep up with the workflow.</p>
        <p class="text-large">The problem isn't you. It's that real estate workflows were designed by people, for people — and they don't scale. You need automation that handles the routine, so you can handle the relationships.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════
       Section 3: What We Automate
       ════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="section" id="what-we-automate">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="re-automate__header animate-on-scroll">
        <span class="section-label">What We Automate</span>
        <h2>Every workflow that's slowing you down.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="re-automate__grid stagger-children">
        <div class="card re-automate__card">
          <div class="card__icon" style="width:32px;height:32px;">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="32" height="32" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M21 15a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H7l-4 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h14a2 2 0 0 1 2 2z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="card__title">24/7 AI Leasing Agents</h3>
          <p class="card__text">AI-powered leasing assistants handle prospect inquiries around the clock, answer common questions, schedule tours, and qualify leads automatically. Your team focuses on closing, not fielding routine questions.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card re-automate__card">
          <div class="card__icon" style="width:32px;height:32px;">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="32" height="32" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M22 17H2a3 3 0 0 0 3-3V9a7 7 0 0 1 14 0v5a3 3 0 0 0 3 3zm-8.27 4a2 2 0 0 1-3.46 0"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="card__title">Intelligent Lead Nurturing</h3>
          <p class="card__text">Inbound leads get automatically matched to properties and sent personalized email sequences. Different paths for sellers, buyers, investors, renters. AI learns which prospects are most likely to convert and prioritizes follow-up.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card re-automate__card">
          <div class="card__icon" style="width:32px;height:32px;">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="32" height="32" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M15 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V7Z"/><path d="M14 2v4a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h4"/><path d="M10 9H8"/><path d="M16 13H8"/><path d="M16 17H8"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="card__title">Lease & Document Intelligence</h3>
          <p class="card__text">AI automatically extracts key lease terms, dates, and obligations from lease documents. Closing documents are organized, tracked for signature status, and flagged if something's missing. Nothing gets lost in email, nothing expires unnoticed.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card re-automate__card">
          <div class="card__icon" style="width:32px;height:32px;">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="32" height="32" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><line x1="18" x2="18" y1="20" y2="10"/><line x1="12" x2="12" y1="20" y2="4"/><line x1="6" x2="6" y1="20" y2="14"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="card__title">Smart Rent Pricing</h3>
          <p class="card__text">AI analyzes market data, comparable properties, tenant mix, and occupancy rates to recommend optimal rental prices. Dynamic pricing adjusts over time. Helps you capture maximum revenue without underpricing inventory.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card re-automate__card">
          <div class="card__icon" style="width:32px;height:32px;">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="32" height="32" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14.7 6.3a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.4l1.6 1.6a1 1 0 0 0 1.4 0l3.77-3.77a6 6 0 0 1-7.94 7.94l-6.91 6.91a2.12 2.12 0 0 1-3-3l6.91-6.91a6 6 0 0 1 7.94-7.94l-3.76 3.76z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="card__title">Predictive Maintenance</h3>
          <p class="card__text">IoT sensors + AI predict maintenance issues before they become emergencies. Tenant maintenance requests are automatically categorized, prioritized, and routed to the right contractor. Track status from submission to completion.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card re-automate__card">
          <div class="card__icon" style="width:32px;height:32px;">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="32" height="32" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><line x1="12" x2="12" y1="1" y2="3"/><line x1="12" x2="12" y1="21" y2="23"/><line x1="4.22" x2="5.64" y1="4.22" y2="5.64"/><line x1="18.36" x2="19.78" y1="18.36" y2="19.78"/><line x1="1" x2="3" y1="12" y2="12"/><line x1="21" x2="23" y1="12" y2="12"/><line x1="4.22" x2="5.64" y1="19.78" y2="18.36"/><line x1="18.36" x2="19.78" y1="5.64" y2="4.22"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="card__title">Tenant Communication & Collections</h3>
          <p class="card__text">Rent reminders, maintenance request updates, lease renewal notices — all sent automatically. Tenants can submit requests via email, SMS, or web form. AI tracks collection status and flags late payments. Follow-ups happen without manual intervention.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════
       Section 4: How It Works
       ════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="re-process animate-on-scroll">
        <span class="section-label">How It Works</span>
        <h2>We've done this before. We do it for real estate teams like yours.</h2>
        <p class="text-large">We audit your current workflows: where leads come in, how follow-up happens, where documents get stuck, how properties get listed, how tenant requests are handled. We map the bottlenecks and the manual work.</p>
        <p class="text-large">Then we build automations that handle the routine parts — email sequences, document routing, CRM syncing, listing updates, tenant communication. Your team focuses on closing deals and managing relationships. The software handles the repetition.</p>
        <p class="text-large">After implementation, we stay with you. We monitor performance, adjust workflows as your business grows, and add new automations when you need them. One contact, consistent support.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════
       Section 5: Results
       ════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="re-results__header animate-on-scroll">
        <span class="section-label">Results</span>
        <h2>What changes in practice.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="re-results__grid stagger-children">
        <div class="card re-results__card">
          <h3 class="card__title">Deals Close Faster</h3>
          <p class="card__text">Leads get consistent, timely follow-up. Documents flow smoothly through closings. Nothing sits in someone's inbox. Typical outcome: closings move 1-2 weeks faster because bottlenecks are gone.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card re-results__card">
          <h3 class="card__title">You Don't Lose Leads Anymore</h3>
          <p class="card__text">Every inbound lead gets a prompt response. Nurture sequences keep prospects engaged automatically. You see which leads are warm and ready. More leads convert because follow-up is consistent.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card re-results__card">
          <h3 class="card__title">Tenants Feel Heard</h3>
          <p class="card__text">Maintenance requests are answered faster. Rent reminders are professional and on time. Lease renewals are prompted automatically. Happy tenants renew longer and refer friends.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card re-results__card">
          <h3 class="card__title">Your Team Stops Fighting Emails</h3>
          <p class="card__text">Manual follow-ups, document chasing, CRM data entry — these now happen automatically. Your team has 8-12 hours per week back to focus on relationships, negotiations, and closing deals.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════
       Section 6: The Opportunity
       ════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="re-opportunity animate-on-scroll">
        <span class="section-label">The Opportunity</span>
        <h2>The industry is moving. Fast.</h2>

        <div class="re-opportunity__stats">
          <div class="re-opportunity__stat">
            <span class="re-opportunity__stat-number">97%</span>
            <span class="re-opportunity__stat-label">of real estate professionals now show active interest in AI</span>
          </div>
          <div class="re-opportunity__stat">
            <span class="re-opportunity__stat-number">$41.5B</span>
            <span class="re-opportunity__stat-label">projected AI real estate market by 2033 — up from $2.9B in 2024</span>
          </div>
          <div class="re-opportunity__stat">
            <span class="re-opportunity__stat-number">10+</span>
            <span class="re-opportunity__stat-label">hours saved per week per property manager with the right automation</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="text-large re-opportunity__followup">Constance IT helps real estate teams move fast. We build automations that integrate with your existing tools and processes. No massive overhaul. Just smart improvements that deliver measurable results.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════
       Section 7: CTA
       ════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <CTASection
    headline="Ready to work smarter, not just harder?"
    subtext="Let's talk about what's costing you the most time right now — whether that's lead follow-up, document management, tenant communication, or listing distribution. We can show you what's possible without a massive overhaul."
    source="real-estate"
  />

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* ──────────────────────────────────────
     Real Estate — scoped styles
     ────────────────────────────────────── */

  /* Problem section */
  .re-problem {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .re-problem h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .re-problem p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .re-problem p + p {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
  }

  /* Automate section */
  .re-automate__header {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 640px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .re-automate__header h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .re-automate__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .re-automate__card .card__icon {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  /* Process section */
  .re-process {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .re-process h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .re-process p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .re-process p + p {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
  }

  /* Results section */
  .re-results__header {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 640px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .re-results__header h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .re-results__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .re-results__card .card__text {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
  }

  /* Opportunity section */
  .re-opportunity {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .re-opportunity h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .re-opportunity__stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .re-opportunity__stat {
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    background-color: var(--bg-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .re-opportunity__stat-number {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent-primary-hover);
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .re-opportunity__stat-label {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .re-opportunity__followup {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  /* Responsive */
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .re-automate__grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }

    .re-results__grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }

    .re-opportunity__stats {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }

    .re-opportunity__stat-number {
      font-size: 3rem;
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .re-automate__grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
